    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455-a4">

                <pb facs="0551" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr.
                            Mariscal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-01-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to my note of the 14th
                    instant, regarding the imprisonment at Matamoros of Messrs. H. C. Harding and H.
                    E. Dugat for infraction of the fiscal laws, I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that a telegram from the consul at that place informs me that this
                    case is still unsettled and the accused persons still in prison.</p>
                <p>I trust that this matter may receive such prompt action as the case may
                    justify.</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
